I see that in `setup_game`, when creating card objects, the code copies `keywords`, `card_types`, and `colors` to the object, but NOT `subtypes`:

```rust
obj.colors = colors.clone();
obj.name = card_name.clone();
obj.keywords = card_data.keywords.clone();
obj.card_types = card_data.card_types.clone();
// subtypes are NOT copied!
```

So `obj.subtypes` remains empty (`Vec::new()`) for regular cards. Subtypes are only stored in the registry (via `card_data().subtypes`) for regular cards.


Now I'm checking how lands are handled when the `PlayLand` action is processed in the engine to see if the same issue occurs there.

