content.thinking:
So Island and Mountain have `subtypes: vec!["Island".into()]` and `subtypes: vec!["Mountain".into()]` in their `CardData`, but these subtypes are accessed via the registry, not stored on the game object (`GameObject.subtypes`).

Now, looking at `setup_game`:
```rust
obj.keywords = card_data.keywords.clone();
obj.card_types = card_data.card_types.clone();
// subtypes are NOT copied!
```

And in the `controller_has_matching_land` function, only `o.subtypes` (the game object's runtime subtypes) is checked, NOT the registry's `card_data().subtypes`:


The function iterates through all objects on the battlefield controlled by the player, checking if any of them have "Island" or "Mountain" in their subtypes, but since basic lands don't have their subtypes copied from the card data during setup, this check will always fail. I should also look at how `clifftop_retreat.rs` handles this to see if there's a pattern I'm missing.

